{
  "_id": "james1",
  "book": {
    "_id": "james",
    "title": "James",
    "titleShort": "James",
    "titleOfficial": "THE GENERAL EPISTLE OF",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "James",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God—Resist temptation—Be doers of the word—James explains how to recognize pure religion.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Israel, Twelve Tribes of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "JST James 1:2 … many afflictions;"
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Temptation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "GR approval by trial. TG Opposition; Test."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "TG Patience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Perfection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2,
            "text": "D&C 42:68; JS—H 1:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Guidance, Divine; Learn; Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Benevolence; Revelation."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "GR reproaches, censures."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Prayer."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "GR doubting, hesitating. TG Doubt."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For let not that man think that he shall receive any thing of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A double minded man is unstable in all his ways.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 18:21; Ps. 12:2; Hosea 10:2. TG Integrity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the brother of low degree rejoice in that he is exalted:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Matt. 23:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the rich, in that he is made low: because as the flower of the grass he shall pass away.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "Isa. 40:6–8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the sun is no sooner risen with a burning heat, but it withereth the grass, and the flower thereof falleth, and the grace of the fashion of it perisheth: so also shall the rich man fade away in his ways.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "GR beauty of its appearance."
          },
          {
            "start": 176,
            "end": 180,
            "text": "1 Tim. 6:17 (17–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "1 Pet. 3:14. TG Blessing."
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "JST James 1:12 … resisteth temptation … TG Steadfastness."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "TG Test."
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Exaltation; Reward."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted of God: for God cannot be tempted with evil, neither tempteth he any man:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG God, Perfection of."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "TG Evil."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But every man is tempted, when he is drawn away of his own lust, and enticed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Temptation."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Lust; Motivations; Sensuality."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it is finished, bringeth forth death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Sin."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Do not err, my beloved brethren.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Ps. 85:12."
          },
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Moro. 7:12 (12–13)."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "John 3:27; 2 Cor. 9:15. TG God, Gifts of."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "D&C 67:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "D&C 67:4, 9."
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "TG God, Perfection of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Of his own will begat he us with the word of truth, that we should be a kind of firstfruits of his creatures.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Prov. 17:27."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "TG Patience."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore lay apart all filthiness and superfluity of naughtiness, and receive with meekness the engrafted word, which is able to save your souls.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Filthiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "GR overabundance of malice, trouble, evil."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "TG Meek."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "GR implanted, ingrafted."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Commitment; Duty; Good Works; Hypocrisy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Luke 6:49 (47–49)."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "1 Cor. 13:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For he beholdeth himself, and goeth his way, and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG God, Law of."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "TG Liberty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If any man among you seem to be religious, and bridleth not his tongue, but deceiveth his own heart, this man’s religion is vain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Gossip; Profanity."
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "GR useless, deceptive, erroneous."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 123
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Charity."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "D&C 44:6. TG Benevolence; Good Works; Welfare."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Deut. 26:13; Job 22:9; 31:21 (21–22); Ps. 10:14; 146:9 (1–10); 3 Ne. 24:5; D&C 136:8 (7–9)."
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "TG Widows."
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "TG Affliction."
          },
          {
            "start": 139,
            "end": 148,
            "text": "1 Tim. 5:22; 1 Jn. 5:18; D&C 59:9. TG Chastity."
          },
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 157,
            "text": "JST James 1:27 … the vices of the world."
          },
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 163,
            "text": "TG Worldliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 122
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
